From 41b1b66613c7bed8639ac5fd0543d9d8cff14861 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 23:01:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09315/11362] Check a window against the planner's vocabulary
 before spending a token on it

GAP-6260 layer 1. An induced engine is only useful if the planner can drive it, and the
planner's move set is `_model_candidates`: actions 1-5 plus a click. A window whose
observed actions fall outside that set teaches the engine transitions the planner will
never ask for, so the engine can score a perfect cell_recall on its own window and still
be unplannable.

lp85 is the measured case. Every action in its cached window is 0 (RESET), and its induced
engine produced ZERO novel successors from the planning root -- 37 nodes, exactly one
candidate sweep of no-ops, the win predicate never consulted, queue exhausted far under
budget. Six A/B cells across both arms were spent on it. The cell_recall was honest; what
it measured was not gameplay.

This is the cheap half of the two-layer discriminator. It costs no engine calls and no
generation, so it runs BEFORE induction rather than diagnosing the wreckage after. The
second layer -- does the induced engine yield a novel successor from the root -- needs an
engine and is not implemented here.

REPORTS, DOES NOT BLOCK. It records the offending actions and warns, then induces anyway,
because refusing to induce is a live-path behaviour change that wants its own measurement
first. Degenerate input yields no finding rather than an exception, since this sits on the
live path and must never itself be the reason induction fails.

The vocabulary constant mirrors `_model_candidates` so the check can run without a grid,
and a test asserts the two agree -- a drifted constant would pass windows the planner can
no longer drive, which is the failure this exists to catch. Asserted rather than
commented, per tonight's repeated lesson that a design property stated only in prose is
one nobody can see break.

13 new tests, including every cached window in the corpus as a negative and the lp85 shape
as the positive. Verified the phase-2 pin is unaffected: the pinned worktree does not
carry this helper.

